In article <1992Oct29.005719.10122@DIALix.oz.au> rswa@DIALix.oz.au
(Radio Spares) writes:

>I've made it to the first level of hell (on level 31), but I don't seem
>to have any means to get any further. I have intrinsic teleport, but as
>far as I can tell (I've searched the whole level) there are no level
>teleporters on the first level of hell.

Intrinsic teleport is really not what you need.  What you need is
teleport control.  If you don't have this, it wouldn't matter if you
had found a level teleport trap or not.

>So you say, go back through the dungeon til you get a scroll of
>teleportation and read it whilst confused. (BTW: does this let you
>teleport levels?).

Yes, it does, as does reading a cursed scroll of teleportation.
Zapping yourself with a wand, casting a spell, or using ^T while
confused do *not* work.

>The problem with this is that I cannot get back past the castle
>level. When going up the stairs from level 31 to the castle I always
>arrive at the back of the castle. I have no way of crossing the moat
>(no water walking or levitation) so I have to go through the castle.
>The trouble is there are at least two trapdoors, each time I try and
>cross them I fall into them and back to level 31. Sigh. There are no
>boulders around to push into the holes either.

You've got a problem.  What you could do is find a potion of
levitation, but that would be too obvious.  You might polymorph into
some monster with intrinsic levitation, like a Vampire Lord, a
floating eye, or some such.  That would only be a viable option if you
had polymorph control and some way to polymorph yourself.  You might
also quaff a cursed potion of gain level on the castle level.  (You'll
still gain a level, it'll just be a different kind of level.)

>Would this work. Wait until an Umber Hulk appears on level 31 (I
>guess it will happen sometime) let him confuse me and then
>control-T??

No, as I said earlier, it won't.

